tps://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk/page/?title=P%2EE&pid=120","https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk/_site/data/files/pupil-premium/sport-premium/8BAF0D61333960A1E75A1EB480089A21.pdf?pid=71","https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk/_site/data/files/pupil-premium/sport-premium/99AE11EF1DDA6013478628957DDC4CC0.pdf?pid=71","https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk/page/?title=Primary+PE+and+Sport+Premium&pid=71","https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk/calendar/?calid=3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10&pid=0&viewid=79&event=5348","https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk/_site/data/files/pupil-premium/sport-premium/8CD0A4A1E1DA6F61E78BD5BBB844780E.pdf?pid=71"],"pageCache":[{"url":"https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk","finalUrl":"https://www.tannersbrookpri.org.uk","fetchedAt":"2026-09-20","contentLength":77101,"contentHash":"5ba9cf6efb92edac75de919f070f8c8dbc5d110d2535cf0e30b2f4aaa0c7e898","textHash":"aab72d2b6599484dd3c9ab7f5c1d7d0b605d6b9cec0f639ce9f09c4eaf23b5a2","pageTitle":"Tanners Brook Primary School - Home","section":"homepage","text":"Think, Believe, Persevere, Succeed\nWelcome\nIngrid Dowse Co-Headteacher\nI am proud to be the Co-Headteacher of Tanners Brook Primary School and to play a part in the education and development of our wonderful children. Having been a member of the Tanners Brook family since 2006, I have had the privilege of serving the school in a variety of roles \u2013 as a teacher, Year Leader, Vice Principal and Co-Headteacher.\nTanners Brook holds a very special place in my heart, not only professionally but personally too, as all three of my children attended the school. This gives me a deep appreciation of the unique community we have here and the positive impact the school has on the lives of our children and families.\nI feel incredibly fortunate to be part of such a vibrant and caring school, where I have the pleasure of watching our children grow in confidence, develop their talents and flourish throughout their time with us. They are supported every step of the way by a passionate, dedicated and highly skilled staff team who are committed to providing the very best opportunities and life chances for every child.\nTogether, we strive to create an environment where every child feels valued, inspired and empowered to achieve their full potential.\nView our Vision & Values\nSarah Mack Co-Headteacher\nI am incredibly proud to be the Co-Headteacher of Tanners Brook Primary School and to continue my journey within a community that I have been privileged to serve for many years, first as a teacher and then as a member of the leadership team. During my time here, I have seen first-hand the dedication of our staff, the support of our families and, most importantly, the achievements of our wonderful children.At the heart of everything we do is our vision: striving for our personal best to make our community proud. We believe that every child can achieve great things and we support this through our shared values of Think, Believe, Persevere and Succeed. Our vision and values help our children grow into confident, resilient and caring individuals who are ready for the opportunities and challenges ahead, both in school and beyond.Together with our families, we have created a nurturing environment where children are encouraged to dream big, work hard and celebrate their successes. I feel immensely lucky to be a part of the Tanners Brook team and look forward to continuing to inspire our community to reach their full potential.\nLatest News\nUpcoming Events\nFriday 25 September 2026\nIndividual & Sibling School Photos\nFriday 25 September 2026\nAfter School Karate\nMonday 28 September 2026\nSchool Nurse Clinic\nFriday 02 October 2026\nAfter School Karate\nTuesday 06 October 2026\nParent Meeting - Senior School\nFriday 09 October 2026\nAfter School Karate\nMonday 12 October 2026\nSchool Nurse Clinic\nFriday 16 October 2026\nAfter School Karate\nFriday 23 October 2026\nAfter School Karate\nMonday 26 October 2026 \u2013 Friday 30 October 2026\nHalf Term\nSat